    "message": "fix(ui): the two tokens whose display depends on inbox config (K-20108)\n\nThe K-20145 fix removed the leaf/recovery refs but left two tokens that\nare findable-but-invisible for the same reason: whether the row shows them\nis a property of how the inbox is configured, not of the row.\n\n`blockedVariantLabel(variant)` was indexed unconditionally, justified in\nthe code and the design guide as \"rendered by the group header the row is\nbucketed under\". That header is only rendered when grouping is not \"None\",\nand \"None\" is the default (`Inbox.tsx:822`). So on the default view, 10\nof the 12 server reasons indexed a group label the row never printed:\n\n  type \"Needs attention\"  -> 4 rows match -> each reads \"Unassigned\n                              blocker\" / \"Parked blocker\" / \"Cancelled\n                              blocker\" / \"Review without action path\"\n  type \"External wait\"    -> 1 row matches -> reads \"External owner action\"\n\nOnly `blocked_chain_stalled` and `blocked_by_uninvokable_assignee` are\nimmune, and only by coincidence: their reason label happens to equal their\nvariant label. The other 10 reasons are a real regression against master,\nwhich indexed no variant label at all. Same lie K-20145 was opened for,\nreached through the other door.\n\n`groupLabel` is now a caller-supplied context token, passed only when the\ngroup header actually renders, and `ownerLabel` is the name the row\nresolves and draws rather than the raw `attention.owner.label`, which is\nnull on the finding-driven path while the row still shows the assignee\nname from `owner.agentId` -- so a displayed name was unfindable.\n\nSuppression also stops being a bare label allowlist. It now tests all\nthree conditions the design guide promised (\"the action carries no\ntarget\"): known fallback label AND `leafIssue` null AND canonical detail\nstring. A label-only rule would have swallowed a real target the moment\nthe server attached one to a stalled chain -- `Assign blocker` -> K-20119\nand `Resume parked blocker` -> K-20035 already do this today, which is\nhow the distinction was found. The guide's three re-open conditions were\ndescriptive; they are now implemented, so the doc and the function\ncannot drift.\n\nVerified: 41/41 targeted tests green (was 35). Pins reproduced by\nreversion, not asserted: re-adding the four leaf/recovery lines fails\n1 test and re-removing the groupBy guard fails 1 more. An independent\nprobe that renders a 7-reason x 2-presentation matrix and mechanically\nasserts every indexed token appears in the DOM goes 10/15 red at 766236100\nand 15/15 green here. `tsc --noEmit` error set is byte-identical to the\nparent commit (58 pre-existing, none in touched files).",
